# SRG-APP-000745-AU-000120  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must implement the capability to centrally review
# and analyze audit records from multiple components within the system.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000745-AU-000120
group:           V-263558
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-003821
control_rev5:    AU-6

contribution:    Splunk aggregates records from multiple components by receiving them on
                 its own inputs and makes them centrally reviewable by granting the
                 reviewing role search access to the indexes that hold them; where the
                 indexers are separate instances, distributed search extends the same
                 review across them.

governs:         authorize.conf - Used to create roles.
governs:         inputs.conf - Configures inputs, distributed inputs such as forwarders, and file system
                 monitoring.

check:           inputs.conf [splunktcp] present
check:           authorize.conf [role_<roleName>] srchIndexesAllowed non_empty

external:        The scope of coverage - which devices and hosts must be aggregated - is
                 organization-defined and recorded in the site security plan, as the
                 product STIG SPLK-CL-000100 fix text states.
external:        Each sending component must itself be configured to forward and must be
                 permitted by the network to reach the receiving port; that configuration
                 lives on those components and on the network.
external:        Where the indexers are separate instances, distsearch.conf
                 [distributedSearch] servers must name them; in a single-instance
                 deployment there are no search peers and its absence is not a finding
                 against this instance.

citation:        inputs.conf.spec:626 [splunktcp], :770 [splunktcp://[<remote
                 server>]:<port>], :876 [splunktcp-ssl:<port>]; authorize.conf.spec:67
                 [role_<roleName>], :292 srchIndexesAllowed = <semicolon-separated list>;
                 distsearch.conf.spec:29 [distributedSearch], :81 servers =
                 <comma-separated list>. Product STIG SPLK-CL-000100 fix and check text.
finding:         Assessed at the application layer alone: Splunk has no receiving input for
                 records from other components, or the role that performs audit review is
                 not allowed to search the indexes holding them, so records from multiple
                 components cannot be centrally reviewed and analyzed in the application.
